commit 718530db11b00586c4fbebc2ddd00b8631f3d278
Author: morty649 <enugulamaruthi@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 30 23:33:07 2026 +0530

    Fix actor gradient starvation and add parallel env + device helpers
    
    The previous 500k-step run regressed (return 71 -> 20) because the actor head
    never trained. Root cause: a single global clip_grad_norm_(0.5) squashed the
    actor head's gradients ~100x (head grad norm ~17 vs encoder ~2468), so the
    policy weights moved <0.002 over the entire run and the policy stayed at its
    initialization.
    
    Changes:
    - train_ppo.py: split the optimizer into three param groups -- encoder at base
      lr, actor head at ACTOR_LR_MULTIPLIER (8x), critic at CRITIC_LR_MULTIPLIER
      (0.2x). Loosen MAX_GRAD_NORM to 1.0, lower entropy to 0.005 and value coef
      to 0.25. Add terminal_reason / episode_completion logging.
    - Add parallel_env.py: spawn-based multi-worker MetaDrive vector env.
    - Add device.py: CUDA/MPS/CPU auto-detection with diagnostics.
    - env.py: macOS offscreen-camera workaround, MSAA off, custom RGB camera.
    - Add SESSION_NOTES.md documenting the diagnosis and the Kaggle render issue.
    
    Evidence: 17% route completion at 20k steps vs 5% for the old 100k policy.

